  "unresolvedAiThreads": [
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6cBCfT",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3851614345,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Automation/VAA.EAPI.Automation.Trips/Tests/Holidays/GraphQL/Documents/RetrieveHolidayBookingDocumentDetailsTests.cs",
      "line": 123,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1742#discussion_r3851614345",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "These assertions check `document.ContainsKey(\"documentDownloadLink\")`, but the test query payload no longer requests `documentDownloadLink`, so the field can never appear in the response regardless of schema support. This creates a false sense of coverage for the legacy-field removal.\n\nEither remove this assertion, or make it meaningful by issuing a GraphQL request that *does* query `documentDownloadLink` and asserting the server rejects it.\n\nThis issue also appears on line 207 of the same file.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Removed both documentDownloadLink absence assertions. The shared GraphQL request does not select that field, so its absence from the response could not verify schema removal; the automation tests continue to validate the replacement documentToken contract and token-based document retrieval."
    }
  ],
